[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
This is arguably a bug in the original C code (it should pass [38;5;10mSPX_N * 8[0m), but since the test vectors are generated from the C reference implementation, the Rust translation must reproduce this exact behavior.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translator "helpfully" added the [38;5;10m* 8[0m multiplication to make it semantically correct:[0m[0m
